Product Requirement Document (PRD): Cohort Leads CRM
Version: 2.0 Product Owner: Rohan Mishra (Mastry.in) Target Platform: Web Application (React Frontend + Google Sheets Backend) 

1. Executive Summary
The goal is to build a comprehensive CRM tailored for managing leads in cohort-based courses. The system will bridge a user-friendly React web interface with a Google Sheets backend to provide a low-cost, high-efficiency solution for tracking learner applications, automating communications, and managing sales team assignments.
2. User Personas & Roles
SuperAdmin/Admin: Full system access, capable of managing settings, users, and all data.
Sales/Advisor: Focused access to assigned leads, scheduling calls, and updating lead statuses.
System (Automated): Performs background tasks like qualification, assignment, and cleanup.
3. High-Level Architecture
The system operates on a decoupled architecture to ensure ease of use and data accessibility:
Frontend: A React Web Application serving as the User Interface (UI) for the team.
Database: Google Sheets acts as the primary database, storing leads, programs, cohorts, and logs.
Logic Layer: Google Apps Script handles server-side logic, including automations, triggers, and API connectivity.
Authentication: Google OAuth 2.0 ensures secure access using existing organizational Google accounts.

4. Functional Requirements
4.1 Lead Management
Centralized Database: Storage of all lead details including demographics, source, and verification status.
Visualization:
Kanban View: A drag-and-drop interface for moving leads through pipeline stages (e.g., New Lead -> Applied -> Eligible).
Table View: A list view for bulk data analysis and filtering.
Lead Actions:
Create, edit, and soft-delete leads (moved to Trash).
De-duplication: Automatic merging of duplicate leads based on phone numbers, preserving the history of sources.
Filtering: Search and filter by status, source, assignee, or program.
4.2 Automation & Logic
Qualification Engine: Automatically determines if a lead is "Eligible" or "Not Eligible" based on application form responses and predefined rules (e.g., negative keywords, numeric thresholds).
Round-Robin Assignment: Automatically distributes new eligible leads among active Sales/Advisor users to ensure balanced workloads.
Status Automation: Changing a lead's status can trigger background actions, such as sending emails or webhooks.
4.3 Program & Cohort Management
Program Definition: Ability to define course details, pricing options, and eligibility criteria.
Cohort Tracking: Manage specific batches (Cohorts) with start/end dates, capacity limits, and application deadlines.
Status Indicators: Visual cues for cohorts that are "Open," "In Progress," or have deadlines approaching.
4.4 Communication & Notifications
Email Integration:
Send automated emails based on status changes (e.g., "Interview Confirmation").
Use HTML templates with dynamic variable replacement (e.g., Lead Name).
WhatsApp Integration:
Trigger WhatsApp messages via Aisensy using mapped templates.
Internal Notifications:
In-app alerts for advisors when leads are assigned to them.
4.5 Sales Operations & Logs
Activity Logging: A complete audit trail of every action taken on a lead (created, assigned, status changed, commented).
Comments System: internal notes with support for Markdown and user mentions.
Call Scheduling: Integration with scheduling tools (Trafft) to track "Sales" or "Interview" calls.
Payment Tracking: Record full payments or installments, including due dates and transaction IDs.
4.6 Form Builder
Dynamic Forms: A built-in builder to create application forms linked to specific programs.
Conditional Logic: Support for showing/hiding fields based on previous answers.
Response Storage: All form submissions are linked directly to the Lead record.

